{
  "summary": "Replaces outbound full-relay peers that do not relay transactions with peers that do, operating only outside of initial block download and when not in -blocksonly mode. To prevent connection drops below outbound targets, the node initiates an extra full-relay outbound connection before evicting a non-relaying peer. Peers that do not relay transactions are excluded from chain-sync eviction protection, though the sole connection to any specific network is preserved.",
  "problem": "Outbound full-relay slots can be occupied by peers that decline transaction relay (such as nodes running in -blocksonly mode). This degrades transaction broadcast and propagation topology without the node operator's knowledge, and nodes with feefilter mismatches or blocksonly peers can be left with too few transaction-relaying outbound connections.",
  "evidence": [
    "Resurrects and reworks #28538 to address previous review feedback, motivated by longstanding open issues #16418 ('Ensure we have sufficient transaction-relay peers') and #28371 ('Seek more/different peers when ours all have too high feefilter')."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Includes a cleanup commit renaming CConnman::ForEachNode to ForEachFullyConnectedNode and removing redundant disconnected-peer checks at call sites.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Initial patch evaluation; the diff directly implements the strategy previously described without approach changes.",
  "card": "Replaces outbound full-relay peers that do not relay transactions with peers that do, ensuring nodes maintain expected transaction relay capacity and diversity. To avoid dropping below outbound connection targets, an extra outbound connection is established before evicting the non-relaying peer, and non-relaying peers are denied disconnect protection unless they are the sole connection on a reachable network. The replacement mechanism is disabled during initial block download and when running with -blocksonly, addressing issues #16418 and #28371 by resolving design feedback on #28538.",
